# Transub Engine

Independent local ASR / machine-translation engine for [Transub](https://github.com/dlsandy/Transub).

- **HTTP API** (`/v1/*`) — primary path used by the Transub desktop app
- **CLI** — debug, CI, and scripting (`serve`, `health`, `run`, `models`)
- **Free translation** — ASR then local Opus NMT (en/ja/ko/de/es/fi/sv→zh), not Whisper `translate`
- Models live under `{engine}/models/{asr|mt|vad}/` (override with `TRANSUB_ENGINE_HOME` / `TRANSUB_ENGINE_MODELS`)

## Quick start

```bash
python -m venv .venv
# Windows: .venv\Scripts\activate
pip install -e ".[dev]"

# Stub mode (no GPU / no heavy models) — for contract tests
set TRANSUB_ENGINE_STUB=1
python -m transub_engine serve --host 127.0.0.1 --port 8765

# CLI
python -m transub_engine health
python -m transub_engine run --media sample.wav --task transcribe --out ./out
```

Real inference extras:

```bash
pip install -e ".[asr-sensevoice,asr-whisper,mt]"
python -m transub_engine models download --profile balanced
```

Optional **Advanced film audio enhance** (Demucs vocal separation; large first-run download):

In Transub: 设置 → 环境 → Transub Engine → **下载 Demucs**  
(with an NVIDIA GPU this also installs **CUDA PyTorch cu124** for GPU separation).

Or manually:

```bash
pip install -e ".[audio-separate]"
# GPU separation (recommended when NVIDIA is present; force-reinstall replaces CPU torch):
pip install --upgrade --force-reinstall torch torchaudio --find-links https://mirrors.aliyun.com/pytorch-wheels/cu126/ --no-index
```

Job fields: `audio.denoise` (`light`, free), `audio.filmAudioEnhance` / `audio.separate` (Advanced, gated by Transub). Full VAD knobs under `vad.*` — see [docs/api-v1.md](docs/api-v1.md).

## FFmpeg

Place binaries under the engine checkout (preferred):

```
_internal/bin/ffmpeg.exe
_internal/bin/ffprobe.exe
```

The engine resolves this path automatically. Overrides: `FFMPEG_BINARY`, `TRANSUB_ENGINE_HOME`.

## Standalone dist (Windows, no system Python)

On a build machine with this repo’s `.venv`:

```bat
dist.bat
:: or: dist.bat --clean --zip --smoke
```

Produces `dist/transub-engine-{version}/` with an **embeddable CPython** under `runtime/` and only the HTTP-stack dependencies (FastAPI / uvicorn / …). Target PCs do **not** need Python installed.

| Path | Role |
|------|------|
| `runtime/python.exe` | Bundled interpreter (`pip` included for on-demand extras) |
| `serve.bat` | Start `http://127.0.0.1:8765` |
| `transub-engine.cmd` | CLI wrapper |
| `models/` | Empty placeholders — download weights on demand |
| `_internal/bin/` | FFmpeg if present at build time |

**Transub nesting:** copy the folder (e.g. `Transub/engine/`), then spawn:

```text
{home}\runtime\python.exe -m transub_engine serve --host 127.0.0.1 --port 8765
```

`TRANSUB_ENGINE_HOME` is optional when using that `runtime\python.exe` (home is auto-detected). Ready check: `GET /v1/health`. Before real jobs, use Models download and (NVIDIA) `ensure-gpu` — they `pip install` into the bundled `runtime/`.

ASR / MT / VAD / CUDA are **not** preinstalled in this minimal shell. Dev-only source tree (needs local Python): `python scripts/build_dist.py --source-only`.

## API

See [docs/api-v1.md](docs/api-v1.md). Compatibility: `apiVersion` major must match Transub’s expected major (currently `1`).

